{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And if harm befalls him, and you bring down my gray hairs</b> — if harm befalls him like his brother, you will bring down my gray hairs in sorrow to Sheol. Or [understand] \"and if harm befalls him\" — that harm may befall him because he is a tender youth, inexperienced in traveling on the road, as he said above (Genesis 42:4), \"lest harm befall him.\" For the meaning of אָסוֹן is a fatal occurrence — [such as] death at the hands of men or a vicious beast, or through a change of the air on the road."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {0 "In the second interpretive option, the phrase שֶׁיִּקְרֶנּוּ כֵן is rendered as 'that harm may befall him,' understanding כֵן as referring back to אָסוֹן; the construction is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:50.845969484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}